/* The bar glyph is app chrome, not a skinnable surface. The base bar rule is
   "no button chrome"; the app owns the soft open-state plate. Painting it
   here with state.selected.fill made the Wi-Fi icon a primary-filled block. */

/* ── Bluetooth popover — REQ-009 ────────────────────────────────────────────
   The bar-anchored Bluetooth popover is a layer-shell surface, so its chrome
   is `surface.panel` (never `surface.window`, never the unconsumed
   `surface.overlay` role). Connected cards are cards, flat paired/nearby rows
   are cells, actions are controls, the Connected badge is a pill, and the
   adapter/footer text is ink/type. Widths, spacing, section separators and the
   connected/scanning semantic signals stay in `../ags-bar/style.css`: this
   template paints roles only and adds no outer inset (the app's sections own
   their 16 px insets — the REQ-007 extra-inset lesson). */

window.bluetooth-popup {
  color: {{SKIN_INK_INK}};
  font-family: {{SKIN_TYPE_FONT_FAMILY}};
}

.bt-surface {
  background-color: {{SKIN_SURFACE_PANEL_BG}};
  border: {{SKIN_SURFACE_PANEL_BORDER_WIDTH}} solid {{SKIN_SURFACE_PANEL_BORDER}};
  border-radius: {{SKIN_SURFACE_PANEL_RADIUS}};
